Z||000000||JBGehling||10-17-2000||10:02 PM||||Hey, <BR>Here's some pictures of my '88 GT (sorry about the quality, I transfered them from a digital video camera, to a quicktime movie, and then to a .gif) I'll see if I can post some better pics one day soon...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/back...fastback.gif"> <P>Unfortunately it's automatic...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/inside.gif"> <P>(the car really doesn't look like this bland color (this is due to the .gif format))<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/side.gif"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/front.gif"> <P>Again, it looks WAY better than these pics show... I'll try to get better pics soon...<BR>Josh<BR>I'm lovin' every minute of it (also, if anyone's ever looking to sell an '87 GT with T-tops and five-speed, I'd love to make a go at it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">)<P>||||reg||10
Z||000001||Black88GT||10-17-2000||10:52 PM||||JB, does your car have Beechwood interior or Gray?  If it has gray, are those wheels stock?  If so, that is pretty rare optioned, I read somewhere (I think it was a '88 dealer selling guide) that it said "Gold lace wheels option, highly recommend Beechwood interior package"<P><BR>just for curiousity's sake....<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
Z||000002||JBGehling||10-17-2000||11:07 PM||||Hey Jeff,<BR>    Ya' got me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. I just painted the wheels gold a few weeks ago (they don't really appear gold in these pictures, but they are a bright gold) from the stock black. And the interior is, indeed, grey. If anyone's interested, I also have some pictures of my '88 formula.<BR>Josh||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||10-17-2000||11:15 PM||||While it is unusual for a gray interiored '88 GT to have gold wheels, there are quite a few out there like that.  RossT's '88 GT has gray leather and gold wheels and I saw a black GT w/gray interior & gold wheels.  I have also seen several tan interiored GT's with black wheels.<P>It depended on who was doing the ordering.  A customer buying a new one could order it any way he wanted.  The gold wheel option was recommended, but not mandatory.<P>Kind of interesting.  I personally like tan interiored GT's to have gold wheels and gray with black, but that's just my opinion.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>  ||||reg||1
